{"title":"Pharma/Animal Nutrition Executive Roadmap","role":"Pharma/Animal Nutrition Executive","summary":"A Pharma/Animal Nutrition Executive works at the intersection of veterinary science, animal health products, pharmaceuticals, feed, supplements, and livestock nutrition. The role may involve technical sales, product management, veterinary product support, feed advisory, customer education, market development, and scientific communication.","facts":{"Current degree":"BVSc & AH (Veterinary Science & Animal Husbandry)","Course":"Veterinary Science"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Pharma/Animal Nutrition Executive works at the intersection of veterinary science, animal health products, pharmaceuticals, feed, supplements, and livestock nutrition. The role may involve technical sales, product management, veterinary product support, feed advisory, customer education, market development, and scientific communication."},{"type":"p","text":"A BVSc & AH graduate has a strong advantage because they understand animal physiology, pathology, pharmacology, microbiology, nutrition, disease management, and livestock production."},{"type":"p","text":"The exact scope depends on the employer. A graduate may work in pharmaceutical companies, animal-health companies, feed manufacturers, veterinary nutrition companies, dairy/poultry businesses, distributors, or technical marketing teams."},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"A BVSc & AH is a professional veterinary qualification. However, a Pharma/Animal Nutrition Executive is primarily an industry/commercial/technical role. Independent veterinary practice, diagnosis, prescription, and treatment must follow applicable veterinary registration and professional regulations."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Career Track","Typical Work"],"rows":[[{"text":"V